course: dictionary
lesson: 489
title: One word, many meanings: ash
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words wear more than one coat. The word ash can mean a grey powder left after something has burned, a kind of tree, or fine dust thrown out by a volcano. Context tells you which meaning is wanted. «In AD 79 the volcano Vesuvius buried the town of Pompeii in ash» is about dust, because a volcano is what buries a town.
explain: Read the words around the word. «In winter, bark, buds and shape still tell trees apart: ash has black buds» tells you ash is a tree, because the sentence is about telling trees apart. Ask yourself what the sentence is about, try your meaning in it, and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Plurals can change the feel of a word. «Families try hard to follow the wishes of someone who has died, such as where their ashes are scattered.» Ashes here means what is left after a person's body has been burned, and scattered tells you it is being spread out. The plural form, ashes, is the one you will usually meet in this sense.
fact: Ash is a noun, and its plural is ashes.
fact: «Ash» can mean the grey powder left after something has burned, as in «wood ash».
fact: «Ash» can also mean a kind of tree with grey bark, as in «an ash tree».
fact: «Volcanic ash» is fine rock dust thrown out by a volcano.
fact: Burning changes materials for ever, so the ash left behind cannot be turned back into what it was: this is an irreversible change.
exercise: Dad scooped the wood ash out of the stove. What does ash mean here? | * Grey powder left after something has burned | Fine rock dust from a volcano | Black buds on a winter branch | A kind of tree with grey bark
exercise: «Ash has black buds, and beech has long pointed buds.» What is ash in this sentence? | Dust thrown out by a volcano | Grey powder left after a fire | The remains of a person | * A kind of tree
exercise: «In AD 79 the volcano Vesuvius buried the town of Pompeii in ash.» Find and copy one word that tells you where the ash came from. | buried | Pompeii | * volcano | town
test: «A volcano is an opening in the crust where melted rock, gas and ash escape from inside the Earth.» What does ash mean here? | A thin mist rising from the sea | * Fine rock dust blown out of the Earth by a volcano | Grey bark on a tree | Black buds in winter
test: «Families try hard to follow the wishes of someone who has died, such as where their ashes are scattered.» What does the plural ashes refer to? | * What is left of a person after their body is burned | A kind of tree | Grey powder in a stove | Dust from a volcano
exam: Which sentence uses ash to mean a tree? | The ashes were scattered by the sea | The grey ash from the fire was cold | * The tall ash in the park had black buds in winter | Ash fell over the town after the eruption
